@startuml 06-component-diagram-architecture
title Aftercare Workbench — Component / Architecture Diagram

actor "Office Admin /\nTechnician / Manager" as User

package "Browser (no build step)" {
  [index.html]
  [styles.css]
  [app.js\n(vanilla ES module)] as AppJS
}

package "Node process — server/index.js\n(zero npm dependencies)" {
  [HTTP + static file server] as HTTP
  [reference.js\npolicy config] as Reference
  [triage.js\nrules engine] as Triage
  [classifier.js\nvoice-intake stub] as Classifier
  [store.js\nin-memory + persistence] as Store
  [data.js\nseed data] as Data
}

database "data/tickets.json" as JSONFile

User --> AppJS : uses (mouse / keyboard / mic)
AppJS --> HTTP : fetch() JSON over HTTP\n(same-origin, CSP-restricted)
HTTP --> Store : listSites / getSite /\nlistTickets / createTicket / updateTicket
HTTP --> Classifier : classifyIntake(transcript, sites)
HTTP --> Reference : read fault types, priorities,\nparties, states, thresholds
Store --> Triage : triage(site, report, history)
Triage --> Reference : read rule inputs
Store --> Data : seed on first boot
Store --> JSONFile : read / write-through persistence
Classifier --> Reference : (fault type ids)

note bottom of AppJS
  Renders all customer-supplied text as
  DOM text nodes, never innerHTML — closes
  off stored XSS from fault descriptions
  or voice transcripts.
end note

note bottom of Triage
  Pure function: (site, report, history) -> decision.
  Same inputs always produce the same
  party / priority / chargeable outcome.
end note

note bottom of Classifier
  Deterministic regex/keyword stub.
  Swappable behind the same interface
  for a real ASR + LLM pipeline later
  (see docs/PRD.md §9).
end note

@enduml
